# Stratocracy — Git LFS tracking
#
# Unreal writes its assets as opaque binaries. Git cannot diff or merge them,
# so every save of an asset stores another full copy in history. Everything
# listed here is routed to LFS instead: the commit stores a ~130-byte pointer
# and the blob lives in the LFS store.
#
# `-text` on every line is load-bearing, not decoration: this repo is used
# with core.autocrlf=true, and without it Git would attempt end-of-line
# conversion on binary content.
#
# Types that .gitignore excludes outright (*.obj, *.dll, *.lib, *.exe, *.a)
# have no rule here — a filter on a path Git never sees is dead weight that
# reads as if those files were tracked. Types .gitignore excludes only under
# a specific path (*.png and *.tga under SourceArt/) do have rules, because
# they are tracked everywhere else.
#
# The `lockable` attribute is deliberately NOT set. It would make every
# matching file read-only in the working tree until `git lfs lock` is run,
# which is the right trade for a team and pure friction for a solo project.
# Add it to the *.uasset and *.umap lines if a second person joins.

# --- Unreal assets -----------------------------------------------------------
# *.uasset also matches *_BuiltData.uasset, which .gitignore excludes; the rule
# is inert there and correct if a BuiltData file is ever force-added.
*.uasset filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.umap   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.ubulk  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.uexp   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.uptnl  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

