# --- Vendored rules module (GDD §4.11 row 9, §4.9) ---------------------------
#
# Source/StratRules/ is vendored verbatim from the stratocracy-crew repo by that
# repo's sync_stratrules.py, and T-INT-01 asserts a byte-for-byte sha256 identity
# between each file here and `cpp_reference/<same name>` at the recorded commit.
# With core.autocrlf=true a checkout would rewrite these to CRLF while the crew
# blob stays LF, and T-INT-01 would fail on a fresh clone for a reason that has
# nothing to do with the sources. `-text` disables that conversion. These are NOT
# LFS files -- they are ordinary text that must survive round-tripping unchanged.
Source/StratRules/** -text

# --- Vendored data tables (GDD §4.8) -----------------------------------------
#
# Data/ holds the §4.8 CSVs, vendored from the crew repo by that repo's
# sync_stratdata.py, plus the manifest recording their sha256 at the source
# commit. T-DATA-05 compares the imported DataTable rows against these bytes, and
# the manifest's hashes are recomputed from the crew object store, so the same
# autocrlf hazard the rule above exists for applies here for the same reason: a
# fresh clone would check these out as CRLF while the crew blob stays LF, and the
# comparison would fail for a reason that has nothing to do with the data.
Data/** -text
